('use_of_english_0325', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Expensive'' is closely associated with sumptuous, not its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Desirable'' is a positive quality consistent with sumptuous, not its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Lavish'' is a direct synonym of sumptuous.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option opposite in meaning to the underlined word(s).

Some people consider the leather upholstery and thick rugs a bit

sumptuous.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "expensive", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "desirable", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "lavish", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "simple", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Sumptuous'' means luxurious and lavish; its opposite is ''simple''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0326', 'Use of English', 'Appropriate word choice', 'Word Choice in Context', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "kxwnre"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Concerned reasons'' is not idiomatic English.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Plenty'' requires ''of'' before a noun (''plenty of reasons''), so ''for plenty reasons'' is ungrammatical.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Myriad of'' without an article is non-standard; the idiomatic forms are ''a myriad of'' or simply ''myriad reasons''.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

I am writing to you for ....... reasons?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "concerned", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "several", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "plenty", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "myriad of", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', '''Several reasons'' is the natural, grammatical phrase; ''myriad'' would need to be used without ''of'' or with an article (''a myriad of''), and ''plenty'' needs ''of'' before the noun.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0327', 'Use of English', 'Vowels', 'Vowel Sounds', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "namskj"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Bear'' has the /eə/ diphthong, a different sound.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Pear'' also has /eə/, not /ɪə/.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Fair'' has /eə/ as well, the same different sound as bear and pear.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that has the same vowel sound as the one represented by the letter(s) underlined.

b

ee

r', '[{"label": "A", "text": "bear", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "pear", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "fair", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "pier", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Beer'' has the /ɪə/ diphthong. ''Pier'' shares this exact sound (in fact, ''beer'' and ''pier'' rhyme).', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0328', 'Use of English', 'Idiomatic expressions', 'Figures of Speech', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "lwt4xp"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Step from step'' is not a standard English phrase.", "misconceptionId": "memorized_not_understood"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Steps after steps'' is not the correct fixed idiom.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Steps by steps'' incorrectly pluralizes both nouns in the fixed phrase.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

Tsadu always cautions that difficult jobs should be done .......?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "step from step", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "step by step", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "steps after steps", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "steps by steps", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', '''Step by step'' is the fixed idiom meaning gradually and methodically, fitting how difficult jobs should be approached.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0329', 'Use of English', 'Appropriate word choice', 'Historic/Historical', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "2ae5n3"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Historical'' means ''relating to history'' generally, not ''significant in history'', so it doesn''t fit an event marking a new beginning.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Historicity of the'' is an awkward abstract noun phrase that doesn''t fit grammatically as an adjective before ''event''.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''History of the'' turns the sentence into an incomplete noun phrase rather than describing the event itself.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

The ...... event marked the beginning of a new life for the entire cabinet?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "historical", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "historicity of the", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "historic", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "history of the", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', '''Historic'' means significant in history (a historic event), while ''historical'' means merely relating to history in general -- a different meaning needed here.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0330', 'Use of English', 'Vocabulary', 'Spelling', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "k8pk3y"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Unkept'' is not a recognized English word -- a common confusion with ''unkempt''.", "misconceptionId": "memorized_not_understood"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Unwashed'' specifically means not washed, a narrower and different claim than being untidy.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Uncleaned for'' is an awkward, non-idiomatic construction.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

In spite of Shade''s good looks, her hair is always ...... ?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "unkept", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "unkempt", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "unwashed", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "uncleaned for", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', '''Unkempt'' is the correct word for untidy hair; ''unkept'' is not a standard English word.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0331', 'Use of English', 'Sentence structure', 'Word Order', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "mecosf"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "Places the material ''wooden'' before the participle ''carved'', reversing the correct order.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "Places the opinion adjective after the material entirely, badly out of order.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "Places the participle ''carved'' before the opinion adjective ''attractive'', reversing the correct order.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

The first prize was ....... tray?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "a carved wooden attractive", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "a wooden attractive carved", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "an attractive carved wooden", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "a carved attractive wooden", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Standard English adjective order places opinion before participle/shape before material: ''an attractive carved wooden tray''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0332', 'Use of English', 'Grammatical usage', 'Tense', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "hbp4zb"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "B", "explanation": "''Could return'' expresses past ability/possibility, not a completed prior action.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Should return'' expresses obligation, not what actually happened before the gates closed.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Would return'' expresses future-in-the-past intention, not a completed prior action.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

Is it true that Okoro ........ when the gates were closed?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "had returned", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "B", "text": "could return", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "should return", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "would return", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Okoro''s return happened before another past event (the gates closing), requiring the past perfect: ''had returned''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0333', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Bad'' is vague and doesn''t specifically reverse the unfriendliness of a sour look.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Satisfactory'' describes adequacy, not the friendliness dimension being tested.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Sinister'' intensifies the negative meaning rather than opposing it.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option opposite in meaning to the underlined word(s).

Idris gives me a

