look every time I pass by him.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "bad", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "satisfactory", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "friendly", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "sinister", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'A ''sour look'' is an unfriendly expression; its opposite is ''friendly''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0334', 'Use of English', 'Idiomatic expressions', 'Sentence Interpretation (Idiom)', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "91ez3x"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Desires to assert his will'' is close but frames it as a wish rather than the demonstrated firmness the idiom actually describes.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Makes his mark wherever he goes'' is a different idiom about leaving an impression, not asserting firmness in a decision.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "The idiom describes firmness, not oppressing others.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Select the option that best explains the information conveyed in the sentence.

The man puts his foot down whenever he is convinced of his action?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "He desires to assert his will in the situation", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "He makes his mark whereever he goes", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "His attitude demonstrates someone who likes to oppress others around him", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "He demonstrates firmness of character", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Puts his foot down'' is an idiom meaning to act with firm decisiveness, i.e. he demonstrates firmness of character.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0335', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Synonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "r0mfcp"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'medium', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Creditable'' means praiseworthy, a different quality from being essential.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Respectable'' also concerns reputation, not essentiality.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Laudable'' means praiseworthy, again a different quality from being essential.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the

