role in the political and economic development of Africa.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "creditable", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "crucial", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "respectable", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "laudable", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', '''Vital'' means essential; ''crucial'' is its nearest match.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0336', 'Use of English', 'Stress', 'Word Stress', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "stfgmb"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Impound'' is stressed on its second syllable (im-POUND), matching the others.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Subject'' as a verb is stressed on its second syllable (sub-JECT).", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Canoe'' is stressed on its second syllable (ca-NOE).", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that has a different stress pattern from the others.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "impound", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "subject (verb)", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "canoe", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "knowledge", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Impound'', ''subject'' (verb), and ''canoe'' are all stressed on the second syllable. ''Knowledge'' is stressed on the first syllable, the odd one out.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0337', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Synonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "r0mfcp"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'medium', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Inevitable'' means unavoidable, an unrelated meaning.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Wonderful'' describes quality, not the inability to express something in words.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Unbearable'' means intolerable, a different concept from being indescribable.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word(s).

The greatness of the creator of the universe is always

inexpressible

to many adherents of certain faiths?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "inevitable", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "wonderful", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "unbearable", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "ineffable", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Inexpressible'' means unable to be put into words; ''ineffable'' is the precise literary synonym for this.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0338', 'Use of English', 'Grammatical usage', 'Noun Modifiers (Singular Attributive Nouns)', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "1gp2vz"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "Wrongly adds a possessive apostrophe and misspells ''soldiers''.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Childish'' means immature, a different word from the noun modifier ''child''.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "Using the plural ''children'' as a modifier before another noun is a common but incorrect overgeneralization from normal plural rules.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

The Secretary-General was shocked at the number of...... ?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "child''s soildiers", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "childish soldiers", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "children soldiers", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "child soldiers", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'A noun used attributively before another noun stays singular: ''child soldiers'' (like ''car parks''), not ''children soldiers''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0339', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Synonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "r0mfcp"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'medium', 'none', '[{"option": "B", "explanation": "''Rampant'' implies uncontrolled spread with a stronger negative connotation than the neutral ''common'' here.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Ordinary'' addresses unremarkableness, not the frequency/widespread sense ''common'' has in this context.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Cogent'' means convincing, an unrelated meaning.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the

option nearest in meaning

to the word or phrase underlined.

The

common

practice among some media practitioners is to be sensational in their reporting.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "prevalent", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "B", "text": "rampant", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "ordinary", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "cogent", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Here ''common'' means widespread/frequent, which ''prevalent'' captures precisely, rather than ''ordinary'' (which describes quality, not frequency).', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0340', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Deluded'' means holding false beliefs, an unrelated quality to motivation.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Disillusioned'' is close but centers on lost belief/idealism rather than the drained energy that opposes ''motivated'' most directly.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Immature'' is an unrelated quality, not the opposite of being motivated.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option opposite in meaning to the underlined word(s).

