('use_of_english_0341', 'Use of English', 'Idiomatic expressions', 'Sentence Interpretation (Idiom)', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "91ez3x"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "B", "explanation": "This describes exactly what being a ''pawn'' would mean, the opposite of what the sentence states.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "This directly contradicts the ''not'' in the original sentence.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "Nothing in the sentence suggests they enjoyed political games.", "misconceptionId": "guessed_no_reasoning"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Select the option that best explains the information conveyed in the sentence.

The men were not pawns in someone else''s political game.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "The action they executed was their idea", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "B", "text": "The men used someone else''s plan", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "They were used by someone''s political game", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "They loved playing political games", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'A', '''Pawns in someone else''s game'' means being used/controlled by others; being told they were NOT pawns means their actions were their own idea.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0342', 'Use of English', 'Grammatical usage', 'Tense & Aspect', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "h5mkn9"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "Using ''will'' in a time clause after ''until'' is a common but incorrect overgeneralization of future-tense marking.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Stopped'' (past tense) doesn''t fit a statement about the future.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Has stopped'' is grammatically possible but ''stops'' is the standard simple-present form expected in this construction.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

